e or an alternate approver.\\n\\nQuick next-step options (pick one)\\n1) Delegate: I coordinate with HR/Comms to finalize and send on behalf of the Admin team.\\n2) Placeholder draft: I prepare a generic admin announcement and route it for approval (no detailed content needed from Mirela).\\n3) Close request: We pause until Mirela or another contact is available.\\n\\nIf choosing 1 or 2, please provide just these basics:\\n\u2022 Category (policy update, facilities/maintenance, office event, holiday/closure, benefits, other)\\n\u2022 Audience (company-wide or specific group)\\n\u2022 Timing (date/time, timezone)\\n\u2022 Channel (email, Slack/Teams, intranet, all-hands slide)\\n\u2022 Approver (name/title) if not Mirela\\n\\nReady-to-use templates (you/approver can choose one and fill in brackets)\\n1) Facilities maintenance\\nSubject: Facilities maintenance on [date/time]\\nBody: Hi everyone \u2014 Building maintenance will occur on [date/time] at [location/floor]. Expected impact: [e.g., elevator downtime/HVAC noise]. Duration: [X hours]. Please plan accordingly. For urgent needs, contact [name/email]. Thank you for your patience.\\nSlack/Teams: Heads-up: Facilities maintenance at [location] on [date/time] for ~[Xh]. Possible [impact]. Questions: [contact].\\n\\n2) Office closure/holiday\\nSubject: Office closed [date] for [holiday]\\nBody: Our [city] office will be closed on [date] for [holiday]. Remote work is [allowed/optional/not required]. Badge access is [open/restricted]. We\u2019ll reopen on [date]. For urgent facilities issues: [contact]. Enjoy the holiday!\\nSlack/Teams: Reminder: [city] office closed [date] for [holiday]. Reopens [date]. Urgent issues: [contact].\\n\\n3) Benefits enrollment reminder\\nSubject: Action required: Benefits enrollment ends [deadline]\\nBody: Open enrollment closes on [deadline time, TZ]. Enroll or make changes at [portal/link]. After the deadline, changes generally aren\u2019t allowed until qualifying events. Need help? Join a Q&A on [date/time] or contact [benefits@\u2026].\\nSlack/Teams: Enrollment ends [deadline]. Do it now at [link]. Help: [date/time] or [contact].\\n\\n4) All-hands logistics\\nSubject: All-hands on [date/time, TZ] \u2014 agenda + links\\nBody: Please join our all-hands on [date/time]. Agenda: [1-3 bullets]. Join link: [link]. Recording will be posted to [location]. Add questions in [Slido/Doc link].\\nSlack/Teams: All-hands [date/time, TZ]. Agenda: [bullets]. Join: [link]. Qs: [link].\\n\\n5) Policy update\\nSubject: Policy update: [policy name] effective [date]\\nBody: We\u2019ve updated the [policy name]. Summary of changes: [bullets]. Effective [date]. Action required: [if any]. Full policy: [link]. Questions: [owner/contact].\\nSlack/Teams: Policy update: [policy] \u2014 takes effect [date]. Summary + link: [link].\\n\\nDistribution checklist (I\u2019ll handle once approved)\\n\u2022 Draft email + Slack/Teams + intranet post in matching language and tone.\\n\u2022 Localize or time-zone phase as needed; schedule for [time] in [TZ].\\n\u2022 Confirm distribution lists and channel owners; obtain final approval; send/schedule.\\n\u2022 Monitor for questions and route to the right owner; post recording/links if applicable.\\n\\nWhat would you like me to do next\u2014delegate, prepare a placeholder draft, or close for now? If delegating, share the approver\u2019s name or team.', task_completed='partial', outputs={}, thought='', action='finish')], inputs={}, outputs={}, agent_state=<AgentState.FINISHED: 'finished'>, resume_state=None, traffic_control_state=<TrafficControlState.NORMAL: 'normal'>, metrics=Metrics({'accumulated_cost': 0.0459845, 'costs': [{'model': 'openai/gpt-5', 'cost': 0.000799, 'timestamp': 1763430733.7824137}, {'model': 'openai/gpt-5', 'cost': 0.008575000000000001, 'timestamp': 1763430742.1664348}, {'model': 'openai/gpt-5', 'cost': 0.00914275, 'timestamp': 1763430778.0337744}, {'model': 'openai/gpt-5', 'cost': 0.027467750000000003, 'timestamp': 176